#70604
"At a Clearing in the Jungle"
"The faint path from the north opens up here into a moderately sized clearing. 
All at once, you find yourself subject to a dizzying assault on all of your
senses.  Towering trees reach to the sky above you, and from the heights
above, you can see monkeys and birds of all sizes chittering, howling,
chirping and squawking to each other in an exotic cacophany of sound. 
Permeating the air around you, the smells of rare flowers, half eaten fruits,
and damp fur produce a rather undescribable smell.
"
""
