#70618
"The Jungle"
"The trees are not quite as dense in this area leaving more room for smaller
vegetation such as flowers, large ferns, and bushes.  Lying across the ground
is a thick blanket of green and brown leaves that rustle with every moment. 
Smaller animals dwell within the leaf cover hiding from predators on a daily
basis while searching for food.  High above, the forest ceiling composed of a
dense cover of leaves has many large gaping holes within the natural roof. 
This provides adequate light to the plants along the forest floor.
"
""
