#70623
"The Jungle"
"A large, weathered pointed rock lies in the center of the blanket of leaves
surrounded by four large trees.  Green moss and fungus cover the face of the
rock and have built up over time.  Gaps between the cluster of trees allow
passage in nearly every direction.  Perhaps the trees are feeling generous to
the traveler to see the wonders of the jungle, yet a trail of fresh blood
droplets dot a path along the leaves to the south.
"
""
