#70628
"The Jungle"
"Water droplets drip from the ferns, pelting the dry leaves below.  Each
droplet quickly disappears, swallowed up by the forest floor.  Screeching
pierces down to the ground from the birds gathered in the trees.  Vines curl
and hang down from the trees like snakes slithering to the ground.  Huddled
together, many of the trees in this area shadow the ferns, bushes, and smaller
plant life, often stealing their sunlight needed to flourish.
"
""
