#70775
"Up in a Tree"
"Standing on an uneven section of the trunk, it takes near perfect balance to
keep from falling out of the tree.  The bark of the trunk is scarred and
marred with many holes chewed into its inner wood layers by insects and small
animals.  Hanging down are many dark green vines like a curtain covering a
window.  From this point, two branches stretch out to the east and west, big
enough for a humanoid to walk across.  Across the other side, a narrow section
allows one to cross to the other side of the trunk.
"
""
