#70776
"A Small Branch's End"
"This branch has stopped its promising growth, ending way short.  Brown and
greenish vines dangle down from the branch like small ropes toward the
ground.  Below the branch is a collection of spear, edged brown rocks
scattered across a small field of ferns.  Littering the branch are colorful
red and green feathers, some matted with dots of dried blood.  Just below a
group of feathers is a tiny dried pool of red blood just at the end of the
branch.
"
""
