#70777
"Along a Branch"
"Droplets of blood dried and fresh blood dot the dark wooden branch as it
twists and curves to the south.  Bits of feathers cling to the branch as
evidence of birds taking rest or making their homes here in the tree.  Vines
and leaves intertwine across the branch making it difficult to fully stand up
without the leaves grasping around the head.  To the south the end of the
branch is visible in a cluster of leaves and vines, while the center of the
trunk looks more comforting to the east.
"
""
