#70778
"The Golden Python's Lair"
"Dried blood mats the branch with large and small feathers clinging tightly to
the end of the branch.  Something appears to have been killed very recently in
evidence to several bloody feathers.  Dense clusters of dark green leaves and
vines in this area of the branch provides several hiding spots for predators
wishing to ambush their prey.  The slight rustling of the leaves around is
almost a solid indication that something is watching every moment made on this
branch very, very closely.
"
