#70782
"Along A Tree Branch"
"The wood of the branch is not only holey but crooked from growth, making
passage on it an act of balance as the branch moves up, down, and to the
side.  Some green leaf clusters are attached to the branch with many leaves
showing signs of insect bites, decay, and animals having torn them off.  White
and greenish bird droppings litter the branch with droplets of blood, some
still fresh.  A couple of the blood droplets run down the branch and trickle
off below onto fallen leaves.  Off to the south, a ghastly view of bones, tiny
pools of blood, and strings of flesh are visible at the branchs end.
"
""
